{
  "id": "elec101-midterm",
  "title": "ELEC 101 \u00b7 Midterm (Labs 4\u20137)",
  "items": [
    {
      "code": "M1",
      "kind": "fix",
      "title": "M1 \u00b7 Find and fix the errors",
      "summary": "A divider drawn badly. Three things on the sheet are wrong: correct them so it matches the paper, then read the output.",
      "vary": {
        "VS": [
          "9",
          "12",
          "15",
          "18"
        ],
        "R1": [
          "1k",
          "1.5k",
          "2.2k",
          "3.3k"
        ],
        "R2": [
          "2.2k",
          "3.3k",
          "4.7k",
          "6.8k"
        ]
      },
      "tasks": [
        "Type your name under the sheet before you start. Your values come from it.",
        "The paper's circuit is VS = DC {VS} volts, R1 = {R1} above R2 = {R2}, with the junction named OUT and the bottom of R2 grounded.",
        "Three things on this sheet are wrong. The open circles and the warnings under the sheet point at them. Fix every one.",
        "Set the analysis to Operating point, run it, and enter the voltage at OUT.",
        "Press Submit exam answer once when you are done."
      ],
      "analysis": {
        "type": "op"
      },
      "useStudentAnalysis": false,
      "circuit": {
        "comps": [
          {
            "type": "V",
            "x": 160,
            "y": 200,
            "rot": 90,
            "label": "VS",
            "value": "DC {VS}",
            "ac": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "R",
            "x": 220,
            "y": 140,
            "label": "R1",
            "value": "470"
          },
          {
            "type": "R",
            "x": 340,
            "y": 200,
            "rot": 90,
            "label": "R2",
            "value": "{R2}"
          },
          {
            "type": "NET",
            "x": 340,
            "y": 140,
            "label": "N1",
            "name": "OUT"
          }
        ],
        "wires": [
          {
            "x1": 160,
            "y1": 200,
            "x2": 160,
            "y2": 140
          },
          {
            "x1": 160,
            "y1": 140,
            "x2": 220,
            "y2": 140
          },
          {
            "x1": 280,
            "y1": 140,
            "x2": 340,
            "y2": 140
          },
          {
            "x1": 340,
            "y1": 140,
            "x2": 340,
            "y2": 200
          },
          {
            "x1": 340,
            "y1": 200,
            "x2": 400,
            "y2": 200
          },
          {
            "x1": 400,
            "y1": 200,
            "x2": 400,
            "y2": 260
          },
          {
            "x1": 400,
            "y1": 260,
            "x2": 340,
            "y2": 260
          },
          {
            "x1": 340,
            "y1": 260,
            "x2": 160,
            "y2": 260
          },
          {
            "x1": 160,
            "y1": 260,
            "x2": 160,
            "y2": 260
          }
        ],
        "seq": {
          "R": 2,
          "V": 1,
          "NET": 1
        }
      },
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "vout",
          "prompt": "Voltage at OUT, in volts",
          "expect": "VS*R2/(R1+R2)",
          "within": "2%",
          "points": 4
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "check": "parts",
          "points": 4,
          "expect": {
            "R1": "{R1}",
            "R2": "{R2}",
            "VS": {
              "dc": "{VS}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "check": "wiring",
          "points": 5,
          "rows": [
            [
              "VS",
              [
                [
                  "R1",
                  0
                ],
                0
              ],
              true
            ],
            [
              "R1",
              [
                [
                  "VS",
                  0
                ],
                "OUT"
              ]
            ],
            [
              "R2",
              [
                "OUT",
                0
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "noOpenEnds",
          "points": 3
        },
        {
          "check": "nodeVoltage",
          "points": 4,
          "node": "OUT",
          "expect": "VS*R2/(R1+R2)",
          "within": "2%"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "code": "M2",
      "kind": "draw",
      "title": "M2 \u00b7 Draw a series circuit and find its bias point",
      "summary": "Draw the circuit from the paper, name its nodes, and report the operating-point voltage between the resistors.",
      "vary": {
        "VS": [
          "10",
          "12",
          "15",
          "20"
        ],
        "R1": [
          "100",
          "220",
          "330",
          "470"
        ],
        "R2": [
          "300",
          "680",
          "1k",
          "1.5k"
        ]
      },
      "tasks": [
        "Type your name under the sheet before you start. Your values come from it.",
        "Draw the paper's circuit: VS = DC {VS} volts, R1 = {R1} and R2 = {R2} in series, with the bottom of R2 grounded.",
        "Name the node at VS's positive side A, and the node between R1 and R2 B.",
        "Put a voltage probe on B.",
        "Run an Operating point analysis and enter the voltage at B.",
        "Press Submit exam answer once when you are done."
      ],
      "analysis": {
        "type": "op"
      },
      "useStudentAnalysis": false,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "vb",
          "prompt": "Voltage at B, in volts",
          "expect": "VS*R2/(R1+R2)",
          "within": "2%",
          "points": 4
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "check": "parts",
          "points": 4,
          "expect": {
            "R1": "{R1}",
            "R2": "{R2}",
            "VS": {
              "dc": "{VS}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "check": "wiring",
          "points": 4,
          "rows": [
            [
              "VS",
              [
                "A",
                0
              ],
              true
            ],
            [
              "R1",
              [
                "A",
                "B"
              ]
            ],
            [
              "R2",
              [
                "B",
                0
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "noOpenEnds",
          "points": 2
        },
        {
          "check": "probe",
          "points": 2,
          "node": "B"
        },
        {
          "check": "nodeVoltage",
          "points": 4,
          "node": "B",
          "expect": "VS*R2/(R1+R2)",
          "within": "2%"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "code": "M3",
      "kind": "draw",
      "title": "M3 \u00b7 DC sweep with a differential probe",
      "summary": "Build the divider again, sweep the source, and measure across R1 rather than to ground.",
      "vary": {
        "R1": [
          "100",
          "220",
          "470",
          "1k"
        ],
        "R2": [
          "300",
          "680",
          "1k",
          "2.2k"
        ],
        "STOP": [
          "10",
          "12",
          "15",
          "20"
        ]
      },
      "tasks": [
        "Type your name under the sheet before you start. Your values come from it.",
        "Draw the paper's circuit: VS (DC 0) feeding R1 = {R1} then R2 = {R2} to ground, with A at VS's positive side and B between the resistors.",
        "Set a DC sweep of VS from -{STOP} to {STOP} in steps of 0.1.",
        "Use the Diff probe to measure A against B, so the plot shows the voltage across R1.",
        "Run it, and enter what that probe reads when VS is at +{STOP}.",
        "Press Submit exam answer once when you are done."
      ],
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "vr1",
          "prompt": "Voltage across R1 when VS is at its most positive, in volts",
          "expect": "STOP*R1/(R1+R2)",
          "within": "3%",
          "points": 3
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "check": "parts",
          "points": 3,
          "expect": {
            "R1": "{R1}",
            "R2": "{R2}"
          }
        },
        {
          "check": "wiring",
          "points": 3,
          "rows": [
            [
              "VS",
              [
                "A",
                0
              ],
              true
            ],
            [
              "R1",
              [
                "A",
                "B"
              ]
            ],
            [
              "R2",
              [
                "B",
                0
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "noOpenEnds",
          "points": 2
        },
        {
          "check": "analysis",
          "points": 3,
          "type": "dc",
          "source": "VS",
          "start": "-{STOP}",
          "stop": "{STOP}",
          "step": "0.1"
        },
        {
          "check": "diffProbe",
          "points": 3,
          "plus": "A",
          "minus": "B"
        },
        {
          "check": "valueAt",
          "points": 3,
          "node": "A",
          "minus": "B",
          "at": "STOP",
          "expect": "STOP*R1/(R1+R2)",
          "within": "3%",
          "label": "The probe reads the voltage across R1 at the top of the sweep"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "code": "M4",
      "kind": "draw",
      "title": "M4 \u00b7 Parametric sweep",
      "summary": "The same divider with R1 stepped through a range, as a parameter rather than a fixed value.",
      "vary": {
        "VS": [
          "10",
          "12",
          "15",
          "20"
        ],
        "R2": [
          "300",
          "680",
          "1k",
          "2.2k"
        ],
        "FROM": [
          "100",
          "200"
        ],
        "BY": [
          "100",
          "200"
        ]
      },
      "tasks": [
        "Type your name under the sheet before you start. Your values come from it.",
        "Draw the paper's circuit: VS = DC {VS} volts into R1, then R2 = {R2} to ground, with B between the resistors.",
        "Place a Parameter part and set RVAL to {FROM}. Give R1 the value {RVAL} so it follows the parameter.",
        "Turn on the parametric sweep and step RVAL from {FROM} by {BY}, three values in all.",
        "Run an Operating point analysis, and enter the voltage at B for the last of the three values.",
        "Press Submit exam answer once when you are done."
      ],
      "analysis": {
        "type": "op"
      },
      "useStudentAnalysis": false,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "vlast",
          "prompt": "Voltage at B for the largest R1, in volts",
          "expect": "VS*R2/(FROM+2*BY+R2)",
          "within": "3%",
          "points": 6
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "check": "parts",
          "points": 3,
          "expect": {
            "R2": "{R2}",
            "VS": {
              "dc": "{VS}"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "check": "wiring",
          "points": 3,
          "rows": [
            [
              "VS",
              [
                "A",
                0
              ],
              true
            ],
            [
              "R1",
              [
                "A",
                "B"
              ]
            ],
            [
              "R2",
              [
                "B",
                0
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "noOpenEnds",
          "points": 2
        },
        {
          "check": "parametric",
          "points": 6,
          "name": "RVAL",
          "from": "{FROM}",
          "to": "FROM+2*BY",
          "by": "{BY}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "code": "M5",
      "kind": "draw",
      "title": "M5 \u00b7 Transient run with a current probe",
      "summary": "A pulse source into a resistor and capacitor. Measure the current through the resistor rather than a voltage.",
      "vary": {
        "V2": [
          "5",
          "9",
          "12",
          "15"
        ],
        "R1": [
          "470",
          "1k",
          "2.2k",
          "4.7k"
        ],
        "C1": [
          "47n",
          "100n",
          "220n"
        ]
      },
      "tasks": [
        "Type your name under the sheet before you start. Your values come from it.",
        "Draw the paper's circuit: a Pulse source VS into R1 = {R1}, then C1 = {C1} to ground. Name the node at the source IN.",
        "Set the pulse to go from 0 to {V2} volts, delay 0, rise and fall 1u, width 1m, period 2m.",
        "Put a current probe on R1: click the part itself, not a wire.",
        "Run a Transient analysis to 2m with a time step of 2u, and enter the peak current through R1 in amps.",
        "Press Submit exam answer once when you are done."
      ],
      "useStudentAnalysis": true,
      "reference": {
        "type": "tran",
        "trStop": "2m",
        "trStep": "2u"
      },
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "ipk",
          "prompt": "Peak current through R1, in amps",
          "expect": "V2/R1",
          "within": "4%",
          "points": 3
        }
      ],
      "checks": [
        {
          "check": "parts",
          "points": 3,
          "expect": {
            "R1": "{R1}",
            "C1": "{C1}",
            "VS": {
              "type": "VPULSE",
              "fields": {
                "v1": "0",
                "v2": "{V2}",
                "pw": "1m",
                "per": "2m"
              }
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "check": "wiring",
          "points": 3,
          "rows": [
            [
              "VS",
              [
                "IN",
                0
              ],
              true
            ],
            [
              "R1",
              [
                "IN",
                "OUT"
              ]
            ],
            [
              "C1",
              [
                "OUT",
                0
              ]
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "check": "noOpenEnds",
          "points": 2
        },
        {
          "check": "analysis",
          "points": 3,
          "type": "tran",
          "stop": "2m",
          "step": "2u"
        },
        {
          "check": "currentProbe",
          "points": 3,
          "part": "R1"
        },
        {
          "check": "extreme",
          "points": 3,
          "part": "R1",
          "which": "max",
          "expect": "V2/R1",
          "within": "4%",
          "label": "The current through R1 peaks where the pulse steps up"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}